  <h1>Code of Conduct &amp; Policies</h1>

  <p>Kin-Fusion is a community gathering built on care, consent, and genuine connection. These agreements help us create a space where everyone — across backgrounds, bodies, and experience levels — can feel welcome and at ease.</p>

  <h2>Consent and Interpersonal Conduct</h2>
  <p>We expect all participants to treat one another with respect and care. This means:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Asking before touching — on the dance floor and everywhere else.</li>
    <li>Accepting "no" gracefully, without needing an explanation.</li>
    <li>Respecting personal space and physical safety while dancing.</li>
    <li>Avoiding hate speech, harassment, or coercive behaviour of any kind.</li>
    <li>Being mindful that our community includes people of all ages, backgrounds, and comfort levels.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Behaviour that harms or threatens others may result in removal from the event without a refund. We trust our community to hold each other with care, and our organizing team is always available to help navigate difficult situations.</p>

  <h2>Reporting Concerns</h2>
  <p>If you experience or witness conduct that feels unsafe or harmful, please reach out to an organizer in person or by email at <a href="mailto:hello@kinfusion.dance">hello@kinfusion.dance</a>. We take all concerns seriously and will respond with care and discretion. You may report concerns before, during, or after the event.</p>

  <h2>Health and Wellbeing</h2>
  <p>We ask that everyone looks out for themselves and for each other:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Please stay home if you're feeling unwell.</strong> If you have cold or flu symptoms, or have tested positive for COVID-19 in the days before the event, please stay home. We'll work with you on a refund — your health and that of our community comes first.</li>
    <li>Up-to-date vaccinations (including COVID and flu boosters) are encouraged but not required.</li>
    <li>Masks are welcome at any time for any reason — please respect anyone who chooses to wear one.</li>
    <li>Hand-washing stations and sanitizer will be available throughout the event space.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Allergens and Food</h2>
  <p>Meals are provided by the event. Our kitchen is <strong>nut-aware</strong> — we ask that you do not bring peanuts or tree nuts onto the property, as we may have participants with nut allergies.</p>
  <p>If you have dietary needs, allergies, or restrictions, please note them in your registration. We'll do our best to accommodate you. For severe allergies, please contact us directly at <a href="mailto:hello@kinfusion.dance">hello@kinfusion.dance</a> before the event so we can plan together.</p>
  <p>You're welcome to bring personal snacks — just please keep nut-containing items to your own camping space.</p>

  <h2>Photography and Video</h2>
  <p>Event photos will be taken throughout the weekend. These may be used on the event website and social media to share the spirit of Kin-Fusion with our broader community.</p>
  <p>If you prefer not to be photographed:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Opt out during registration, and let photographers and organizers know at check-in.</li>
    <li>To request removal of a specific photo after the event, email <a href="mailto:hello@kinfusion.dance">hello@kinfusion.dance</a> — we'll take care of it promptly.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For personal photography: please check with people before posting photos of them publicly, and always remove photos on request.</p>
  <p>Recording a class or workshop requires the instructor's permission.</p>

  <h2>Recreational Substances</h2>
  <p>We're a community of adults and trust participants to make their own choices. We ask that everyone remains aware of how their state affects others and avoids behaviour that makes people feel unsafe or uncomfortable. Organizers reserve the right to ask someone to remain sober for the remainder of the event if their behaviour becomes problematic, and removal without refund is possible in serious cases. This is not a space intended for exploring recreational substances, so we invite you to experience it sober.</p>

  <h2>Refund Policy</h2>
  <p>We understand that plans change. Our refund policy is:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Full refund (100%)</strong> for cancellations received by <strong>August&nbsp;15, 2026</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Partial refund (50%)</strong> for cancellations after August&nbsp;15, 2026.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you become ill (including COVID-19) close to or during the event, please reach out — we'll do our best to work something out. To request a refund, email <a href="mailto:hello@kinfusion.dance">hello@kinfusion.dance</a>.</p>
</div>
